## 6. Fit and cost

- Stack: firstmate and `OllieCrew` are Bash repositories, `knoliver` is Python (`pyproject.toml` only), `fm-sandbox` holds only `README.md` (`ls /home/hugo/firstmate/projects/*`). The npm and lockfile material (`ext SKILL.md:281-302`) has no target here.
- Human-in-the-loop assumptions: a human author who answers questions (`:239`), human review turnaround (`:251-258`), human disagreement resolution (`:260-269`), a human final call (`:221`). Firstmate workers are autonomous and never address the captain (`AGENTS.md:39`).
- Tool availability: `which npm git node` -> `/home/hugo/.local/share/mise/installs/node/26.7.0/bin/npm`, `/usr/bin/git`, `.../node`; `which pnpm yarn` -> not found. No other tools are named.
- Context cost: about 85 tokens of always-loaded description (339 bytes) at any automatic placement, plus about 5,200 tokens per load.
- Who would load it where:
  - Trial-only: only the session given `pi --skill <path>`.
  - User-global `~/.agents/skills` plus `~/.claude/skills`: every Pi and Claude Code session on the machine (Pi `docs/skills.md:61`), including every crew worker in every project.
  - Firstmate `.agents/skills`: every worker in a firstmate worktree.
  - Whether no-mistakes' own review and fix agents load user-global skills is not verified (section 9). If they do, a user-global copy could push `Critical`/`Nit` labels into pipeline review output.
- The harvested piece costs one sentence in a Test-step setting and only the time of one focused test run per new condition. That must stay within `firstmate-coding-guidelines/SKILL.md:115-117`, which forbids suite walks in `commands.test`.

## 7. Recommendation

`harvest`, with one piece. Everything else stays out, and specifically none of the clashes in section 5 may come along: the merge-trigger description, the approval verdict, the stacked multi-model review, "Ask before deleting", running the suite inside review, require-cleanup-before-submission, shape-based presumptive blockers, and the Required/Critical/Nit/FYI labels.

1. Condition-inversion check (from `ext SKILL.md:164`, idea re-derived, no text copied).
   Target owner: the no-mistakes Test step through its supported per-repository setting `test.instructions`, starting with one project's `.no-mistakes.yaml` (firstmate's own file is at `/home/hugo/.no-mistakes/worktrees/3f83383b2e86/01M66J7TBMNGZSZPZQX5FC74XP/.no-mistakes.yaml`, `test.instructions` block). It should not go into a firstmate skill, and the tool's embedded prompt is not replaced; if the trial shows value, also note it for the no-mistakes maintainer.
   One-sentence rewrite: "For each boolean condition the change adds, temporarily invert it in the run worktree, run only the focused test that should cover it, restore the file byte for byte, and report a warning finding naming the missing test case when that test still passes."
   Trial: run it as a separate captain-approved task in `projects/fm-sandbox`. That project has no tests today, so seed one small script and test, set the line on the sandbox's default branch, and validate one change twice, with and without it.
   Pass needs at least one surviving inversion correctly reported as a missing test, restored source with no stray diff, and no full-suite run. Otherwise drop the piece and record this skill as `decline (conflict)`.

## 8. Captain's decision

- A - Harvest the condition-inversion check as one `test.instructions` line, first through a short sandbox trial (recommended).
- B - Decline outright as conflicting with the pipeline's sole ownership of review and with merge authority; nothing is taken.

Recommended: A.

